  "notes": "{呼|よ}び{出|だ}す is a compound godan verb from {呼|よ}ぶ (to call) + {出|だ}す (out).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を particle: 〜を{呼|よ}び{出|だ}す\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {先生|せんせい}に{呼|よ}び{出|だ}される: to be summoned by the teacher\n- {上司|じょうし}に{呼|よ}び{出|だ}される: to be called in by one's boss\n- タクシーを{呼|よ}び{出|だ}す: to call a taxi\n- {思|おも}い{出|で}を{呼|よ}び{出|だ}す: to evoke memories\n\nUSAGE:\nThe passive form {呼|よ}び{出|だ}される is very common, especially in school/work contexts where being summoned often implies trouble.\n\nCOMPUTING:\n{関数|かんすう}を{呼|よ}び{出|だ}す: to call a function",
